e band, prefer the node that consumes more remaining capacity\n    # (larger load pressure), tie-broken by smaller travel distance.\n    secondary = np.where(in_band, -load_pressure + 0.01 * (d_cur / scale), np.inf)\n\n    return int(unvisited_nodes[np.argmin(secondary)])","code_sha256":"8cbe0bb5f8c746937d80af7931dea82e9d889f873d0653a5841c34610692c869","elapsed_seconds":0.203,"error_code":null,"error_detail":null,"evaluation_id":"621e5e63ea044dd68df46d0533669dff","generation_parents":[{"algorithm":"Build a radial \"savings-angle\" priority: for each unvisited node compute its angular detour cost relative to the depot direction using the law of cosines from the triangle (current, node, depot), then blend this detour with a load-aware penalty that rewards consuming capacity near route end, selecting the node that jointly minimizes detour per unit of demand absorbed.","code_sha256":"8f654664c6d84ee3859418c818d8876bf260abc130429710b1c804ec9f869e0f","population_member_indices":[1],"selected_parent_position":0},{"algorithm":"Explicit parent","code_sha256":"1a983cd2775b19da834351006923908b39c89908da6f4d65869141f9193c5b9c","population_member_indices":[0],"selected_parent_position":1}],"generation_request_ref":"rounds/round_0002/eoh_run/results/exchanges/request_10.json","instance_objectives":[0.014054018712122718,0.03148994864354664,-0.02101559031699376,-0.017997756347865813],"lineage_status":"verified","metrics":{"fitness_definition":"mean((raw_objective-reference_objective)/reference_objective)","raw_objectives":[12.014684821008432,10.853754023679954,12.146973140357824,12.261485712831476],"reference_kind":["solver_reference","solver_reference","solver_reference","solver_reference"],"reference_objectives":[11.84817041232914,10.522404060217072,12.407728887420175,12.486209468554943]},"objective":0.0016326551727024472,"origin":"generated","repair_request_ref":null,"revision":"original","suite_hash":"3735556bcd35e48a2980433e0430fbf0a299984320a011ef95af9c549dd5d8d6","valid":true},{"candidate_id":"candidate_4","code":"def select_next_node(current_node: int, depot: int, unvisited_nodes: np.ndarray,\n                     rest_capacity: float, demands: np.ndarray,\n                     distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Select the next node to visit in a CVRP greedy construction.\"\"\"\n    if unvisited_nodes.size == 0:\n        return depot\n\n    d_cur = distance_matrix[current_node][unvisited_nodes]\n    d_dep = distance_matrix[depot][unvisited_nodes]\n    dem = demands[unvisited_nodes].astype(float)\n\n    scale = float(np.max(distance_matrix[depot])) if distance_matrix.size else 1.0\n    if scale <= 0.0:\n        scale = 1.0\n\n    cap = float(rest_capacity) if rest_capacity > 0.0 else 1.0\n    load_pressure = dem / cap\n\n    # Primary score: normalized NN distance, stronger depot foreshortening,\n    # cubic load bonus to favor fuller loads.\n    primary = (d_cur / scale) + 0.25 * (d_dep / scale) - 0.40 * (load_pressure ** 3)\n\n    # Second stage: re-rank within a slightly wider relative band of the best.\n    best = float(np.min(primary))\n    band = max(abs(best), 1e-9) * 0.03 + 1e-6\n    in_band = primary <= best + band\n\n    # Within the band, prefer higher load consumption; penalize longer travel.\n    secondary = np.where(in_band, -0.6 * load_pressure + 0.05 * (d_cur / scale), np.inf)\n\n    return int(unvisited_nodes[np.argmin(secondary)])","code_sha256":"4bef2518fef5f2137bb29bbd0de4ceac57911f079de5c2e01bf77c6be9cf1423","elapsed_seconds":0.219,"error_code":null,"error_detail":null,"evaluation_id":"aea9b4dd76f94af283289d63bc16f204","generation_parents":[{"algorithm":"Blend a normalized nearest-neighbor distance with a depot-return foreshortening term and a squared load-pressure bonus, using a second-stage relative-band tie-break that only re-ranks candidates whose primary scores fall within a narrow window, so the priority behaves like the reference near the nominal scale while still differentiating clustered candi